      "writtenOn": "2023-02-17T01:08:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here\u0027s what I tried when I first implemented this: http://review.skia.org/645059\n\nThere might be parts where AutoEnterStack is missing, since this was written when AutoStack was at PS1 and it\u0027s likely evolved since then.\n\nPassing the pointer is probably better than what I originally did with the stackID accessor, but that\u0027s neither here nor there; I\u0027d probably change it to pointer-passing if we decide to land it.\n\nWhen I wrote it, I felt like the benefit of RAII was super minimal, and I didn\u0027t like the extra scopes everywhere. Forgetting to `stack.exit()` isn\u0027t a minor thing you can forget; it will set the whole program on fire, so it\u0027s not going to save us from an accidental oops (every SkSL test failing will do that).",
      "parentUuid": "c0d75cf9_be330db5",
